1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:04,796
<i>She told me it was your idea</i>
<i>to send this to me,</i>

2
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:08,091
<i>and I couldn't thank you enough.</i>

3
00:00:08,174 --> 00:00:12,095
<i>Melissa is very lucky</i>
<i>to have a father like you.</i>

4
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:14,389
<i>Thank you so much!</i>

5
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:15,515
<i>Thank you, thank you!</i>

6
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:18,143
<i>- It's the best.</i>
<i>- Congratulations, ma'am!</i>

7
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:19,436
[HAZEL] <i>Thank you so much!</i>

8
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:24,023
[BILLY]<i> In a way,</i>
<i>I should actually thank you.</i>

9
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,944
<i>If you hadn't stolen LoveFeast,</i>

10
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>I wouldn't have thought</i>
<i>of something much better.</i>

11
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:33,700
<i>Which one of us is the bigger thief?</i>

12
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:35,994
<i>Why don't you just tell the truth,</i>

13
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,913
<i>so I can understand</i>
<i>where your anger is coming from?</i>

14
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,374
[BILLY]<i> I'm sure she just</i>
<i>came here to spy on us.</i>

15
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:44,669
<i>Hearts Island will be</i>
<i>our next biggest project.</i>

16
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,880
<i>Twenty single women…</i>

17
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,256
[BILLY, JORDAN]
<i>This summer!</i>

18
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:50,008
<i>Pebblng's newest offering?</i>

19
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:53,011
<i>We'll choose 20 women searchers,</i>

20
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:56,639
<i>and we will bring them</i>
<i>to a romantic island</i>

21
00:00:56,723 --> 00:01:00,185
<i>which we'll call Hearts Island.</i>

22
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:03,772
[LINDSAY]<i> Why is this one</i>
<i>a carbon copy of that?</i>

23
00:01:03,855 --> 00:01:07,025
<i>It's called exactly the same!</i>
<i>Hearts Island!</i>

24
00:01:07,108 --> 00:01:10,070
<i>It's a reality TV show</i>
<i>in the US that flopped.</i>

25
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,362
<i>Get out of my office.</i>

26
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,114
<i>And get out of my company!</i>

27
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:15,742
<i>I should've listened to Billy.</i>

28
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:17,744
<i>Billy?</i>

29
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:20,538
<i>Billy this, Billy that! It's always Billy!</i>

30
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,082
<i>You deserve each other!</i>

31
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,835
[PHONE CHIMING]

32
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,264
- [CONFETTI POPS]
- [SHRIEKS]

33
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:40,600
<i>- Surprise!</i>
<i>- Surprise!</i>

34
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:43,311
<i>- Wow! A surprise for me!</i>
<i>- Yes, yes!</i>

35
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:47,315
<i>- Thank you! Oh, thank you!</i>
<i>- Congratulations!</i>

36
00:01:48,942 --> 00:01:51,152
<i>Wow! You actually went all-out!</i>

37
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:53,530
<i>How sweet! Thank you!</i>

38
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:56,324
<i>And, of course,</i>
<i>congratulations to all of us.</i>

39
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:57,617
<i>You stayed.</i>

40
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,160
<i>You fought for us.</i>

41
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:00,912
<i>For LoveList.</i>

42
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:02,455
<i>So I promise,</i>

43
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:05,542
<i>we'll keep making this family stronger.</i>

44
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:09,337
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:13,174
[DOCTOR]
<i>Mr. Toledo is cleared for discharge.</i>

46
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:15,718
<i>He may now be transferred</i>
<i>into your custody.</i>

47
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:16,970
<i>Okay, Doc.</i>

48
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:30,024
Guys, it's only been three days
since Happily Ever After,

49
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:33,611
and memberships are up,
ads are performing.

50
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:36,447
Investor interest is pouring in!

51
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:37,991
- Yeah!
- Yay!

52
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:41,369
Speaking of investors, it's official.

53
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:45,748
The investors Bea stole from us
pulled out of Pebblng.

54
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:49,586
In fact, they're asking to set
a meeting with us!

55
00:02:49,669 --> 00:02:53,464
And even business owners
who are not in our original list

56
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:55,550
are interested in partnering with us!

57
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:57,635
- Wild!
- Nice!

58
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:59,596
We have so much to celebrate.

59
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:03,725
- [BILLY, THEN EVERYONE] Cheers!
- [JORDAN] Cheers to that!

60
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,686
We should celebrate it
along with Jordan's birthday tomorrow.

61
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,396
[TONI] Double celebration!

62
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:10,607
Your and Billy's birthdays are
only a day apart, right?

63
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:13,234
Come on, guys! It's just like old times.

64
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,028
It's a double celebration!

65
00:03:15,111 --> 00:03:17,113
- Yeah! Let's go!
- Guys, no.

66
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,032
- I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
- [CHARM] Hm?

67
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:20,241
I already have birthday plans.

68
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:22,452
- Aww, that sucks.
- [JORDAN] But thank you.

69
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:24,579
- You're the best.
- [CHARM] What a bummer.

70
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,789
But thank you. You guys are
the best. Thank you.

71
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:30,376
- Oh my, oh my!
- What a killjoy.

72
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:41,971
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:03,785
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:04:25,056 --> 00:04:26,349
Sir.

75
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:29,811
Huh?

76
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:37,402
'Bi?

77
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:52,041
These are your things.
I'll wait for you outside.

78
00:04:56,004 --> 00:05:00,717
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,437
[EXHALES]

80
00:05:16,649 --> 00:05:21,112
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

81
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:28,328
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:11,496
- [CALOY GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- [HANDCUFFS RATTLING]

83
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:12,580
What is this?

84
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:17,627
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:18,628
What is it this time?

86
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:22,006
[GRUNTS]

87
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,636
[GROANS]

88
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:29,055
[SHARP STAB]

89
00:06:29,138 --> 00:06:32,266
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [COP GROANING]

90
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,018
- Stop it!
- [METAL TRAY CLANKS]

91
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:37,105
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

92
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:45,029
[SNICKERS]

93
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:52,662
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

94
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:08,302
[GROANING]

95
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:27,280
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,206
[BEA] Hurry up!

97
00:07:40,168 --> 00:07:42,170
I knew you couldn't stay away from me.

98
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,591
We have a lot of work to do.

99
00:07:46,674 --> 00:07:51,554
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:07:51,637 --> 00:07:53,014
[MUSIC FADES]

101
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:55,850
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

102
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,143
'Bi, thank you.

103
00:07:57,810 --> 00:07:59,312
I'll make it up to you.

104
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:01,898
From now on, I'll do all the work.

105
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,942
You don't have to do anything because…

106
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:07,111
- [CALOY EXHALES]
- [GUN CLICKS]

107
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:09,030
Hey, where did you get that?

108
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:10,239
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,782
I got it from the cops.

110
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:16,078
You never learn, do you, huh, Caloy?

111
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,122
You can't use that.

112
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,082
Why not?

113
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:22,168
This will be useful. It still has bullets.

114
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:24,337
Come on, let's use it.
I want to fire it so bad.

115
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,423
I just said that you can't.
Are you out of your mind?

116
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:29,550
Chill out.

117
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:31,010
- What I want…
- [CALOY SIGHS]

118
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:35,598
is just to give that freaking Billy
a fright.

119
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:38,601
She's an animal.
She wanted me behind bars.

120
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:39,894
What an animal.

121
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:44,065
But I don't think it would hurt

122
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:47,026
to give her a proper scare.

123
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:49,237
What do you think?

124
00:08:50,446 --> 00:08:51,489
Hmm?

125
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,409
You want to scare her, babe?

126
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:58,204
I'll take care of it.

127
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,705
[GROANS]

128
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:01,374
I said you can't use the gun.

129
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:02,833
Don't call me babe.

130
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:07,129
- [BIRDS CHIRPING]
- [MENACING MUSIC FADES]

131
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:11,717
[CROWD SINGING, CLAPPING]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

132
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:15,263
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

133
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:18,766
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

134
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:22,019
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

135
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:26,023
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

136
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:30,027
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to me ♪</i>

137
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:31,612
<i>Make a wish, son.</i>

138
00:09:31,696 --> 00:09:33,739
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:09:33,823 --> 00:09:34,949
[BLOWS]

140
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:36,284
<i>- Yay! </i>[CLAPS]
- [JUDE CHUCKLES]

141
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:39,662
[JUDE, JADE CLAPPING]

142
00:09:41,789 --> 00:09:43,416
What's your wish, my dear grandson?

143
00:09:44,458 --> 00:09:45,918
My wish is

144
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,253
long life

145
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,171
for you, Grandpa.

146
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,674
I wish to be with you for a long time.

147
00:09:51,757 --> 00:09:54,010
Oh! But it's your birthday.

148
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,846
Your wish should be for yourself.

149
00:09:56,929 --> 00:09:58,514
You've always put me first. [CHUCKLES]

150
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,765
Don't worry about it, Grandpa.

151
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:01,684
I have another wish.

152
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,019
Hmm?

153
00:10:03,102 --> 00:10:04,562
Happiness for

154
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:07,106
the people I care about most.

155
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:11,652
[MUSIC TURNS BRIGHT]

156
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:13,154
Isn't it your birthday too?

157
00:10:13,237 --> 00:10:15,364
It's tomorrow, Grandpa.

158
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:16,657
[JUDE CHUCKLES]

159
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:19,035
- Come on, blow your candle.
- The three of us should do it.

160
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:20,620
- Together. Let's go, let's go.
- Okay.

161
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,496
One, two, three.

162
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,539
[ALL BLOW]

163
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:24,874
Yay!

164
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:26,584
- [CROWD CHEERS, APPLAUDS]
- Happy birthday!

165
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:29,086
Okay, time to eat!

166
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:31,380
Let's eat.

167
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:35,134
- There's more food there.
- Grandpa!

168
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:36,886
Time to eat.

169
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,512
- [JORDAN] Enjoy all the food.
- Thank you.

170
00:10:38,596 --> 00:10:41,098
You can eat anything you want today!

171
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,100
- Thanks, dude.
- And later, he can have a slice of cake.

172
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:45,061
- I asked permission.
- Eat to your heart's content.

173
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:46,520
Remember. Make some space, okay?

174
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,272
- Cake. Cake.
- Just one slice.

175
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,443
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:55,488
You again?!
I told you not to come back!

177
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:58,449
- Calm down. Grandpa, relax.
- Grandpa, it's okay.

178
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:00,451
Calm down. It's not him.

179
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:02,870
- Nurse, please.
- [NURSE] Let's go.

180
00:11:05,206 --> 00:11:06,624
Grandpa.

181
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:07,750
[JORDAN] Just calm down.

182
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,169
[BILLY] Go ahead and eat, Grandpa.

183
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:15,966
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

184
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:22,765
I thought I already made myself clear
to your manager.

185
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:26,102
We asked that that male nurse
stay away from Grandpa Jude.

186
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:28,437
But according to our manager,
that's just impossible, sir.

187
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:31,023
- He's on duty and just doing his job.
- [SIGHS]

188
00:11:31,774 --> 00:11:33,484
And what about your job to keep him safe?

189
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:35,986
Last week, he slipped in the bathroom.

190
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:38,406
All right, sir. I'll let our manager know.

191
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:40,282
- Excuse me.
- That works best. Thank you.

192
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:41,409
Dude.

193
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,870
[SIGHS]

194
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,080
I'm sorry.

195
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:48,958
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

196
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,301
Happy birthday!

197
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:01,220
I'm sorry, dude.

198
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:03,472
Today was supposed to be fun.

199
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,099
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:07,560
Come on, you don't need to apologize.

201
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:10,271
It's partly their fault too.

202
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:13,899
I get it.
This is Grandpa Jude we're talking about.

203
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:18,362
He's the only family I have left.

204
00:12:20,489 --> 00:12:22,992
I don't think I can handle
losing another loved one.

205
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:25,995
It'd break me, dude.

206
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:31,459
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,715
[MUSIC FADES]

208
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:43,304
[ALL SINGING, CLAPPING]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

209
00:12:43,387 --> 00:12:46,390
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

210
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:49,143
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

211
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:51,061
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

212
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:53,022
- To me!
- [BILLY] Yeah!

213
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:55,191
- Thank you, thank you.
- [BILLY, FRIENDS] Make a wish!

214
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:58,027
[BLAIRE] Aww!

215
00:12:58,110 --> 00:12:59,737
[CHEERING, CLAPPING]

216
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:01,363
Thank you, thank you.

217
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:02,698
[BILLY GIGGLES]

218
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:06,660
After what happened earlier,
I thought we needed a redo.

219
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:08,496
It's still your birthday.
So, happy birthday!

220
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:09,663
- Thank you.
- Happy birthday!

221
00:13:09,747 --> 00:13:11,040
This was supposed to be just for you.

222
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,750
Oh, since when?

223
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:16,003
Ever since we were kids, we've always
celebrated our birthdays together.

224
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:18,797
So it can't be just about me.

225
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:21,509
Okay, guys. It's almost midnight.

226
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,385
So let's start the countdown!

227
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:25,471
- That's right.
- Billy, it's almost your day!

228
00:13:25,554 --> 00:13:28,015
- My birthday! Okay!
- Come on, guys! Let's do it!

229
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:29,850
- Let's do the countdown!
- It's your moment, girl!

230
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:33,062
- [ALL] Five, four, three!
- [BILLY] Here we go!

231
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:35,231
- Two, one…
- This is it!

232
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,315
[JORDAN] Not this one.

233
00:13:36,398 --> 00:13:38,275
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

234
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,401
Oh!

235
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:42,780
[ALL SINGING, CLAPPING]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

236
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:46,283
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

237
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,744
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

238
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,704
- To me!
- [LAUGHTER, APPLAUSE]

239
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:51,997
[JORDAN] To you!

240
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,249
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:56,377
- Thank you! Thank you, guys!
- [WHOOPING, CLAPPING]

242
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,003
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

243
00:13:58,087 --> 00:13:59,171
Let's drink!

244
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,131
- Happy birthday!
- Thank you!

245
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:02,925
[MUSIC FADES, ENDS]

246
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:04,426
- Ms. Val?
- [VALERIE GULPS]

247
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,095
Can you still handle it? Because…

248
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,764
it's starting to look less
like fun drinking.

249
00:14:08,847 --> 00:14:10,266
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

250
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:11,600
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

251
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:13,644
Uh, yeah.

252
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,814
It's… for moving on.

253
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:19,692
Moving on? [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

254
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:24,613
Yeah, well… [SIGHS]

255
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,741
Kevin and I broke up.

256
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:30,452
And I guess we really can't
fake sparks, huh?

257
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,248
Yeah. [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

258
00:14:34,331 --> 00:14:35,541
Agreed.

259
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:37,001
Um…

260
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,086
I agree with you, Ms. Val.

261
00:14:40,379 --> 00:14:45,175
If you're meant to be together,
then you will be. But if not…

262
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,887
I guess it's just not meant to happen.

263
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:51,307
You're so sweet! Thank you!

264
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,183
[VALERIE GIGGLES]

265
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,852
Twinny.

266
00:14:54,935 --> 00:14:56,228
Are you okay?

267
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:58,647
Have some food.
Would you like a slice of cake?

268
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,524
- Come on.
- No, no, I'm good. [CHUCKLES]

269
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:01,984
Thank you.

270
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:02,943
Okay.

271
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:04,737
- Robbie, my love!
- Hmm?

272
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:07,031
- This is for you.
- For me?

273
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:09,325
If it's meant for you,
then you'll have it. Right?

274
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,242
Mm-hmm.

275
00:15:10,326 --> 00:15:11,368
So tell us, bro.

276
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:13,120
When is your wedding taking place?

277
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:14,705
We don't have an exact date yet.

278
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,206
Also, we're avoiding too much pressure.

279
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,417
- We're still saving up.
- Mmm.

280
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,712
But if I were a rich man like you,
we'd marry anytime.

281
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:23,964
- Right, my love?
- You're silly.

282
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:25,090
Anytime, you say?

283
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:26,800
He hasn't even proposed yet.

284
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:27,968
To this day?

285
00:15:28,802 --> 00:15:29,720
Babe.

286
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,513
We'll get there, okay?

287
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:33,933
Let me guess.

288
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:34,892
Soon.

289
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:37,436
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [CHARM] Always soon.

290
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:40,731
Wait a minute. Excuse me.

291
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,442
Uh, hello, Ma?

292
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:46,403
Mm-hmm. Yes, yes.

293
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:47,571
[RALPH] No.

294
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:50,366
- We're working on it.
- Your competition is tough.

295
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,867
- [SOFT THWACK]
- Hey!

296
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:53,243
No, it's fine.

297
00:15:54,244 --> 00:15:55,579
It's true.

298
00:15:58,457 --> 00:15:59,458
Here.

299
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,502
This is your birthday gift.

300
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,796
[BILLY] Hmm.

301
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:06,715
Wow! You're so sweet.

302
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:07,883
Open it.

303
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:11,637
No way.

304
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:15,265
- It's this? You finished it?
- Mm-hmm.

305
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:19,561
[BILLY] Okay. Okay.

306
00:16:20,062 --> 00:16:23,399
<i>I'll hold your hand in the madness</i>

307
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:27,695
<i>Run to me if they cast you aside</i>

308
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:32,908
<i>And if you've lost all drive</i>
<i>I'll be your solace</i>

309
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:37,997
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:39,498
You're making me cry.

311
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,458
[FAKE SOBS]

312
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:42,835
This is beautiful.

313
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:44,878
- It's beautiful!
- Really? You like it?

314
00:16:44,962 --> 00:16:45,921
Super.

315
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,965
Best birthday gift ever.

316
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:50,300
- Happy birthday, dude.
- [BILLY] Thank you.

317
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:53,095
Well, there you have it!
Did you say best birthday gift ever?

318
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:54,972
C'mon, boss. Play it for us!

319
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:57,016
- [CHEERING]
- [BILLY] I'd love that!

320
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:00,978
- It's just my birthday, <i>no </i>big deal.
- [ROBBIE] Yeah, she's right.

321
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:02,146
What?

322
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,690
- [TONI] Go, Jordan!
- It's just us! C'mon!

323
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:06,817
- [YANI] Jordan!
- Indulge me just this once!

324
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,235
[JORDAN] Your day will come, Robbie.

325
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:10,195
[CHEERING]

326
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:15,284
- [ROBBIE] Yo! Wait!
- [CLEARS THROAT]

327
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:17,161
- I'll turn off the lights.
- [TONI] Perfect!

328
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,704
- You don't have to do that.
- [MARJ] Wow!

329
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:21,206
- [TONI] It needs to be bright.
- [CHEERING] Perfect!

330
00:17:21,290 --> 00:17:23,500
- [BLAIRE] Here we go!
- Okay, okay.

331
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:28,589
I wrote this as Billy's birthday gift,
but it's inspired by all of you, so.

332
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:31,133
- This is <i>Sandal.</i>
<i>- </i>[CHEERING] Wow!

333
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:33,552
- [BLAIRE] How touching!
- [TONI] Here we go.

334
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:40,434
<i>♪ When you come home ♪</i>

335
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:43,103
<i>♪ Weighed down and broken ♪</i>

336
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,230
<i>♪ I can tell ♪</i>

337
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:50,527
<i>♪ By the words unspoken ♪</i>

338
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:56,200
<i>♪ So come here by my side ♪</i>

339
00:17:56,950 --> 00:18:02,081
<i>♪ Let's leave the rest</i>
<i>Of the world aside ♪</i>

340
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:07,086
<i>♪ I'll hold your hand in the madness ♪</i>

341
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:12,883
<i>♪ Run to me if they cast you aside ♪</i>

342
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:15,636
<i>♪ And if you've lost all drive ♪</i>

343
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:21,558
<i>♪ I'll be your solace ♪</i>

344
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:25,646
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

345
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:32,694
<i>♪ Let's just dance</i>
<i>To the beat of our hearts ♪</i>

346
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:37,157
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

347
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:44,039
<i>♪ When you're crying and don't know why ♪</i>

348
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:49,378
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

349
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:52,381
[ENRICO] <i>I'll never get tired of asking</i>
<i>for your forgiveness, Billy.</i>

350
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:57,052
<i>I understand why you can't</i>
<i>forgive me right away.</i>

351
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,471
<i>I should've been the one</i>
<i>you could lean on.</i>

352
00:19:00,389 --> 00:19:01,974
<i>But I wasn't there for you.</i>

353
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:03,851
<i>Either of you.</i>

354
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:06,728
<i>I just hope you'll give me another chance</i>

355
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:09,523
<i>to show you how deeply sorry I am,</i>

356
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:11,733
<i>and how much I love you all.</i>

357
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,194
<i>Happy birthday, my Billy.</i>

358
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:15,988
<i>I'm very proud of you.</i>

359
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:23,287
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:36,175
[JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

361
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:38,886
<i>♪ Let's leave the rest</i>
<i>Of the world aside ♪</i>

362
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:42,014
<i>♪ With all its baggage ♪</i>

363
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:44,266
<i>♪ Whatever happens ♪</i>

364
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:46,351
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

365
00:19:46,435 --> 00:19:50,147
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

366
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,024
<i>♪ Lean on me ♪</i>

367
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:56,069
<i>♪ Just lean on me ♪</i>

368
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:58,113
- [CHEERING]
- Okay.

369
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:00,157
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

370
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,367
- Thank you.
- [FRIENDS] That was great!

371
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:08,707
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

372
00:20:15,297 --> 00:20:16,423
<i>I'm on my way to Billy's.</i>

373
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:18,967
<i>Be careful, okay?</i>
<i>You're still wanted.</i>

374
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:23,639
- [LOUD THUD]
- [GROANS]

375
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:27,517
<i>Caloy escaped!</i>

376
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:28,769
<i>What?!</i>

377
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:31,480
- [LINE RINGS]
- <i>C'mon, dude. C'mon!</i>

378
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,650
<i>- Give up already!</i>
- [SCREAMS] <i>Help! Let me go!</i>

379
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:38,028
[ENGINE REVS]

380
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:40,572
<i>- Stop it!</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

381
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:41,990
- [LOUD THUD]
- [GRUNTS]

382
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:46,203
<i>She fought back, so I beat her up.</i>
<i>I slammed her head against the wall.</i>

383
00:20:46,286 --> 00:20:48,080
<i>Why did you hurt her?</i>

384
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,290
<i>He hurt Billy?</i>

385
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:52,501
<i>Serves her right!</i>

386
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:55,337
<i>If one of us gets caught,</i>
<i>we'll all get dragged into this.</i>

387
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:57,881
<i>She's already ruined</i>
<i>every plan you had for us.</i>

388
00:20:57,965 --> 00:21:01,093
<i>That's why what Caloy did</i>
<i>was the right thing.</i>
